{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>As the service of a gift I give you your priesthood.</b> The service of the priesthood that I impose upon you is not a service of contempt but a service of greatness and a gift from Me to you, for it is for you honor and splendor, apart from the fact that you earn your livelihood through it. And the reason He repeated והזר הקרב יומת — 'and the stranger who draws near shall be put to death' — that is, the stranger among the priests, and even a Levite. And the burnt offering of Samuel, who was a Levite, was a temporary ruling (הוראת שעה), like the deed of Gideon the Manassite. And this passage also indicates that it was in the wilderness of Sinai, when the Tabernacle was erected and the Levites were chosen and the firstborn were disqualified."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:45.850524997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}